  "claim_boundary": "count-level correspondence only; the raw L/R Clifford grid is the 6x6 rook scheme, not the W33 spread association scheme",
  "reading": "The 600-cell special Clifford fibrations give 36 L/R cross-pairs. Each cross-pair is two shared great decagons with 20 vertices. Natural vertex-overlap relations split as 180 pairs with overlap 0 and 450 pairs with overlap 4, exactly the same-row/same-column and different-row/different-column relations of a 6x6 grid. The zero-overlap graph is srg(36,10,4,2). W33 spreads instead have overlap profile 270/360 and graphs srg(36,15,6,6) and srg(36,20,10,12). Therefore the raw Clifford L/R count does not supply a canonical spread labeling. The missing object is an extra symplectic selector that twists the 6x6 grid into the W33 spread scheme.",
